course: dictionary
lesson: 4859
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word ibis has two. Its first meaning is a bird: a wading bird with long legs and a long, thin, curved beak that lives near water.
explain: Its second meaning is slang from Australia: the white ibis is called a «bin chicken» because it eats from rubbish bins. Read the words around it. «A scarlet ibis is red because of the red pigments in its crabs and shrimps» is about a bird, because it mentions colour and food.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If the bird meaning fits, the sentence is about a wading bird. Slang is informal, so you will mostly meet «bin chicken» in chatty talk, not in a science book.
fact: An ibis is a wading bird with long legs and a long, thin, curved beak.
fact: Ibis ibises or ibis: the plural can be «ibises» or «ibis».
fact: «Bin chicken» is an Australian slang name for the white ibis, because it eats from rubbish bins.
fact: Scarlet ibises get their red colour from the pigments in the crabs and shrimps they eat.
fact: In ancient Egypt, people thought the ibis was sacred to the god Thoth.
exercise: «Colours and beaks have reasons: a scarlet ibis is red because of the red pigments in its crabs and shrimps.» What kind of thing is an ibis here? | A tall tree on a hill | *A wading bird with long legs and a curved beak | A kind of fish that swims in the sea | A type of rubbish bin
exercise: «Scarlet ibises get their red colour from pigments in the crabs and shrimps they eat.» Where do scarlet ibises get their red colour from? | From rubbish bins | From the sea water | From the bright sun | *From the crabs and shrimps they eat
exercise: Mia reads, «The bin chicken pecked at the rubbish bags behind the café.» What is a bin chicken? | *An Australian white ibis that eats from rubbish bins | A hen that lays eggs in a box | A bin with a picture of a chicken on it | A chicken sold in a shop
test: Sam writes, «The ibis has long legs for wading.» What does wading mean? | *Walking through shallow water | Swimming very fast underwater | Flying high in the sky | Sleeping on a branch
test: «The ancient Egyptians thought the ibis was sacred to the god Thoth.» What does sacred mean? | Dirty and smelly | *Holy, or special to a god | Very fast | Hidden from view
exam: What tells you which meaning of ibis is being used in a sentence? | Whether the word has a capital letter | The page the word is printed on | *The words and sentences around it, which is its context | The number of letters in the word
